-- Review of smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: a property that reads a ledger through a
-- rule, calling it as a genitive. A property is evaluated outside any run, where a
-- RECALL reads nothing, so `l4 explore --always "never taken"` refuses it
-- (exit 1). On unstable the WITH and genitive spellings were not refused:
-- `never taken` held "in every one of the 5 states", exit 0, although
-- `taken` is committed TRUE in some of them.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVEN dflt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is taken` dflt MEANS fromMaybe dflt (RECALL OFFICIAL's `taken`)

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`taken now` MEANS `is taken` FALSE

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `taken now`
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

GIVEN who IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`taken by` who MEANS fromMaybe FALSE (RECALL OFFICIAL's `taken`)

GIVEN taken IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`never taken` taken MEANS NOT (Bob's `taken by`)
